# Trusted base of Acorn: build and gate scripts, Lake package configurations,
# Acorn's own build/verification tools, native C primitive, and GitHub config.
#
# The merge gate refuses a change that touches a path named here unless an admission of it is on
# record (scripts/admission.sh, which reads this file at the commit a change starts from). That
# check accepts only empty lines, lines that start with `#`, and `/path @rbeauchamp` with letters,
# digits, `.`, `_`, `-` and `/` in the path; any other line, another owner included, fails the
# gate run of every change that starts from it. Lake reads a package's `lakefile.lean` before its
# `lakefile.toml`, so both names are listed for both packages, whichever exists.
/scripts/ @rbeauchamp
/lean/lakefile.lean @rbeauchamp
/lean/lakefile.toml @rbeauchamp
/site/lakefile.lean @rbeauchamp
/site/lakefile.toml @rbeauchamp
/lean/AcornTools/ @rbeauchamp
/lean/AcornTools.lean @rbeauchamp
/lean/Bootstrap.lean @rbeauchamp
/lean/os/ @rbeauchamp
/.github/ @rbeauchamp

# The validation pipeline's configuration, which names the command that runs the gate and the
# admission check, and the files that lock the toolchains and the dependencies' commits, which
# select the code of the dependencies' checks (Regula's audit, lean-intent's checks).
/.no-mistakes.yaml @rbeauchamp
/lean/lean-toolchain @rbeauchamp
/lean/lake-manifest.json @rbeauchamp
/site/lean-toolchain @rbeauchamp
/site/lake-manifest.json @rbeauchamp

# What counts as a permitted departure: the closed type of declared departures and the register
# that states each one. The audit that compares them is under /lean/AcornTools/ above. Admitting a
# departure is the owner's and is its own change (docs/learned-only-binding.md).
/lean/Acorn/Provenance.lean @rbeauchamp
/docs/learned-only-binding.md @rbeauchamp

# Statements that missions are to prove, held as Lean definitions of type Prop (targets),
# and the registry that lists them. Each is a frozen contract: a change to one is the
# owner's to make. The directory also holds the pin files of the frame check and the registration
# of the statements of landed missions (lean/AcornTools/Frame.lean).
/lean/AcornVerif/Targets/ @rbeauchamp
